=== is a late-stage ShapeKnots gate affordable? ===
  today, per in-loop solve:      37 pKiss + 33 ProbKnot =    11.84 s   (9.1% of these pass the panel)
  gate, per PANEL-PASSING solve: 11.0 candidates x (same + 1 ShapeKnots) =   130.80 s
  cost per panel-passing solve today:   130.09 s (you must already pay for 11.0 attempts, you just cannot SEE which one worked)
  -> the gate's overhead is only the ShapeKnots calls themselves: 0.71 s per success = 0.5% on top

  NOTE the asymmetry: today the 11 candidates are spread over ~11 separate EXECUTIONS and
  only 21/60 targets ever land one. A gate spends them inside ONE execution, which is why the
  per-execution rate (3.2/60) can move toward the ever-solved rate (21/60) at nearly no extra
  oracle cost -- the search work is already being done and thrown away.
